<title>USA: C-TEC enters $50 mln pact with Lucent.</title>
<headline>C-TEC enters $50 mln pact with Lucent.</headline>
<dateline>PRINCETON, N.J. 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>C-TEC Corp said Tuesday it has entered into a five-year, $50 million agreement for Lucent Technologies Inc to provide telecommunications equipment.</p>
<p>C-TEC said it will use Lucent's 5ESS-2000 switch in New York City and a similar one in Boston to support a subsidiary, RCN Corp.</p>
<p>C-TEC is a telecommunications and high-technology company. Lucent, the former equipment arm of AT&amp;T Corp is based in Murray Hill, N.J.</p>
</text>
